#
# Labels for controversies:
#   "proven"   - convicted, pleaded guilty, admitted, or confirmed by a court or an official investigation
#   "charged"  - indicted or impeached (the outcome is always stated)
#   "alleged"  - reported or claimed but never established by a court or official finding
#   "disputed" - facts are established but whether it was wrong is a matter of real disagreement
#
# Selection rule for controversies: included if it led to an investigation by Congress, an inspector
# general, a special/independent counsel or a court, or was a sustained national controversy covered
# across the political spectrum.

